00:14:16.377 --> 00:14:17.795
Don't be like this.

00:14:17.879 --> 00:14:19.964
Could you please talk to Beauté

00:14:20.047 --> 00:14:21.841
and ask them to drop the lawsuit?

00:14:21.924 --> 00:14:23.968
How am I supposed to do that?

00:14:24.051 --> 00:14:25.636
There's nothing I can do, either.

00:14:26.345 --> 00:14:28.014
[sobbing] Please, Meri.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.810
For old times' sake.

00:14:33.728 --> 00:14:35.271
No... [sniffles]

00:14:35.813 --> 00:14:36.814
You and I...

00:14:38.149 --> 00:14:39.567
We were lovers once.

00:14:40.776 --> 00:14:41.777
Please?

00:14:41.861 --> 00:14:44.197
Why did you have to take things this far?

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.449
What made you take it this far?

00:14:46.532 --> 00:14:47.867
[sobbing]

00:14:54.957 --> 00:14:56.667
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

00:14:58.961 --> 00:15:00.296
[continues sobbing]

00:15:05.551 --> 00:15:06.719
I know.

00:15:09.388 --> 00:15:11.057
I know because I was like that.

00:15:13.142 --> 00:15:14.894
You did this because you hate me.

00:15:20.524 --> 00:15:22.902
Still, you shouldn't have
done this to him.

00:15:25.071 --> 00:15:26.072
[sniffles]

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.201
Wooju.

00:15:32.495 --> 00:15:33.496
These days,

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.374
I'm really happy and at ease.

00:15:38.501 --> 00:15:40.836
I think I like him a lot.

00:15:42.255 --> 00:15:43.381
So...

00:15:44.173 --> 00:15:46.467
I want you to be happy, too.

00:15:48.511 --> 00:15:49.553
[sniffles]

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.475
I wish you'd move on from all this.

00:15:55.017 --> 00:15:58.229
Seeing you broken
and falling apart like this

00:15:58.312 --> 00:15:59.730
doesn't make me happy

00:16:01.107 --> 00:16:02.233
or satisfied.

00:16:02.316 --> 00:16:03.401
[sobbing]

00:16:05.736 --> 00:16:07.530
[♪ heartfelt, melancholy music playing]

00:16:09.031 --> 00:16:11.325
Let's forget that you hurt me

00:16:12.451 --> 00:16:14.120
and your hatred toward me.

00:16:16.706 --> 00:16:18.624
Let's forget it all...

00:16:21.419 --> 00:16:23.504
and just keep the good memories.

00:16:24.672 --> 00:16:25.673
How about that?

00:16:26.716 --> 00:16:28.426
Can you do that for me?

00:16:38.602 --> 00:16:39.979
[sobbing]

00:16:43.441 --> 00:16:46.360
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:16:48.654 --> 00:16:49.905
[digital queue alert chimes]

00:16:52.325 --> 00:16:54.076
FAMILY REGISTRATION

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.661
-Hello.
-[clerk] Hi.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.246
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

00:17:03.002 --> 00:17:04.837
DIVORCE DECREE

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.339
[mouse clicking, keyboard clacking]

00:17:10.301 --> 00:17:11.677
It's been submitted.

00:17:11.761 --> 00:17:12.845
Thank you.

00:17:13.929 --> 00:17:15.389
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

00:17:26.525 --> 00:17:27.610
[sighs in relief]

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:37.203
[sighs deeply]

00:17:45.795 --> 00:17:46.837
[car horn honks]

00:18:13.572 --> 00:18:14.657
Get in.

00:18:26.085 --> 00:18:27.128
[♪ upbeat pop music fades]

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:40.474
This is it
since the house was already furnished.

00:18:40.933 --> 00:18:42.393
-[digital beep]
-Shall we get going then?

00:18:51.152 --> 00:18:52.236
[both sigh]

00:18:52.319 --> 00:18:54.113
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

00:18:54.196 --> 00:18:57.533
So much has happened at this place.

00:19:03.956 --> 00:19:04.957
Let's go.

00:19:26.353 --> 00:19:29.398
Hello, Ms. Yoo Meri.
I'm calling from Beauté Department Store.

00:19:30.274 --> 00:19:31.317
[Meri exclaims]

00:19:32.318 --> 00:19:34.612
Did you not hear from Mr. Baek?

00:19:35.988 --> 00:19:36.989
Pardon?

00:19:37.364 --> 00:19:38.365
A divorce?

00:19:38.949 --> 00:19:41.869
Yes, I got a divorce.

00:19:41.952 --> 00:19:44.079
Because I'm no longer a newlywed,

00:19:44.997 --> 00:19:47.082
I don't have the right to keep the prize.

00:19:47.166 --> 00:19:48.209
[Mr. Kwon] Wait, hold on.

00:19:48.292 --> 00:19:50.419
But we need to transfer the ownership.

00:19:50.503 --> 00:19:52.129
Can't we just give it to you?

00:19:52.213 --> 00:19:55.341
[hesitates] But I'm not fit for it,
so I can't accept it.

00:19:56.133 --> 00:19:57.218
I'm really sorry.

00:19:57.301 --> 00:20:00.054
-[stutters] No, that's not... Ms. Yoo...
-[line disconnects]

00:20:00.137 --> 00:20:01.430
Ms. Yoo... She...

00:20:02.431 --> 00:20:03.766
[stutters] She hung up.

00:20:05.893 --> 00:20:07.561
-Was that Beauté?
-Yes.

00:20:08.187 --> 00:20:10.231
I wonder if Mr. Baek didn't report it.

00:20:10.898 --> 00:20:12.358
Beauté seems to be unaware of it.

00:20:12.441 --> 00:20:15.152
They're chaotic right now
because of the illegal lobbying funds.

00:20:15.236 --> 00:20:17.238
[acknowledging] I saw it on the news.

00:20:18.364 --> 00:20:20.950
Anyway, aren't you sad?

00:20:21.826 --> 00:20:23.077
You mean about the house?

00:20:23.577 --> 00:20:25.704
[inhales deeply] I am.

00:20:26.622 --> 00:20:27.915
I really am.

00:20:29.041 --> 00:20:31.710
When will I ever get to live
in a house like that?

00:20:33.128 --> 00:20:34.129
But...

00:20:34.713 --> 00:20:39.468
I found something
much more precious than that.

00:20:39.552 --> 00:20:40.636
What's that?

00:20:42.888 --> 00:20:43.931
You know what it is.

00:20:44.014 --> 00:20:46.058
I really don't. What is it?

00:20:46.725 --> 00:20:48.018
Never mind if you don't.

00:20:48.102 --> 00:20:49.353
What is it?

00:20:50.354 --> 00:20:51.981
Let's just listen to some music.

00:20:52.064 --> 00:20:53.232
[both chuckle]

00:20:54.191 --> 00:20:55.609
-Okay.
-[digital beep]

00:20:55.693 --> 00:20:57.987
-Play something upbeat.
-[digital beep]

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.738
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

00:20:59.822 --> 00:21:01.031
[chuckles]

00:21:05.411 --> 00:21:07.705
Wow, the sound system is great.

00:21:07.788 --> 00:21:08.956
It's amazing, right?

00:21:09.874 --> 00:21:11.667
-It's quite expensive.
-[both laugh]

00:21:19.633 --> 00:21:20.718
[clatters]

00:21:33.522 --> 00:21:35.900
MANAGING DIRECTOR BAEK SANGHYEON

00:21:43.782 --> 00:21:44.992
-[phone vibrating]
-[clangs]

00:21:48.078 --> 00:21:50.289
YOON JINGYEONG

00:21:51.916 --> 00:21:52.917
Yes, hello?

00:22:03.886 --> 00:22:04.887
[sighs]

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.558
What happened?

00:22:09.642 --> 00:22:10.935
I saw the news.

00:22:13.562 --> 00:22:17.232
Regarding Mr. Kim Wooju,
it'll be swept under the rug.

00:22:18.233 --> 00:22:19.902
If it's revealed
that it was for the bribe,

00:22:20.569 --> 00:22:22.488
the company will also be in trouble.

00:22:23.447 --> 00:22:25.074
So, you don't need to worry about it.

00:22:25.157 --> 00:22:26.533
That's not it.

00:22:29.036 --> 00:22:31.080
I'm worried about you.

00:22:31.914 --> 00:22:33.832
According to the news,

00:22:33.916 --> 00:22:35.376
they said you came clean.

00:22:36.585 --> 00:22:38.754
You told me to pay for my sins
and live without shame.

00:22:39.254 --> 00:22:41.090
When did I say that?

00:22:41.715 --> 00:22:43.300
[chuckling softly] Maybe I heard it wrong.

00:22:43.384 --> 00:22:44.760
What I meant was,

00:22:44.843 --> 00:22:47.137
in the world of crime,

00:22:47.221 --> 00:22:49.098
it's only right
that virtue triumphs over vice

00:22:49.181 --> 00:22:50.599
and justice prevails.

00:22:51.725 --> 00:22:55.646
Well, I was only telling you to take
responsibility for what you did wrong,

00:22:55.729 --> 00:22:57.314
not for the things you didn't.

00:22:57.398 --> 00:22:58.440
[chuckles softly]

00:22:58.816 --> 00:23:00.192
That's what I did.

00:23:00.985 --> 00:23:03.612
I only acknowledged
the things that I did wrong.

00:23:03.696 --> 00:23:05.406
Just like you told me to.

00:23:06.407 --> 00:23:08.784
So, what happens now?

00:23:09.702 --> 00:23:11.620
[inhaling deeply] Well...

00:23:12.121 --> 00:23:13.956
Since I'm under
non-custodial investigation,

00:23:14.456 --> 00:23:16.041
I'm sure they'll reach a verdict soon.

00:23:16.917 --> 00:23:17.960
Don't tell me...

00:23:19.044 --> 00:23:21.755
You're not actually going
to prison or anything, right?

00:23:22.506 --> 00:23:24.425
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

00:23:25.092 --> 00:23:26.135
[sighs softly]

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:29.346
[Sanghyeon sighs in despair]

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:30.723
The night view looks

00:23:31.724 --> 00:23:33.684
especially beautiful tonight.

00:23:40.357 --> 00:23:41.358
I think...

00:23:43.736 --> 00:23:46.947
I'll think of you a lot from time to time.

00:23:51.285 --> 00:23:52.494
[sighs deeply]

00:23:55.789 --> 00:23:57.958
Can I ask you a favor?

00:24:08.886 --> 00:24:09.887
Can you call her?

00:24:10.345 --> 00:24:11.597
Yes, ma'am.

00:24:13.307 --> 00:24:15.267
[Songhee] I think it's better
with the shadows.

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:16.602
-[Meri] Should we try?
-Twenty...

00:24:16.685 --> 00:24:18.145
-[phone ringing]
-Negative 30.

00:24:23.817 --> 00:24:25.402
Yes, this is Yoo Meri.

00:24:25.778 --> 00:24:27.780
-[Philnyun] It's me.
-Pardon?

00:24:28.197 --> 00:24:29.448
Wooju's grandma.

00:24:30.240 --> 00:24:31.325
[gasps]

00:24:32.159 --> 00:24:33.702
Hello, Chairwoman.

00:24:34.411 --> 00:24:36.205
I'm being discharged today.

00:24:36.997 --> 00:24:40.334
So, sometime next week,
let's meet at home.

00:24:41.043 --> 00:24:43.045
Oh, I'm always free.

00:24:43.921 --> 00:24:46.840
I'll come by
if you call me when you're free.

00:24:46.924 --> 00:24:48.509
Yes, thank you.

00:24:48.592 --> 00:24:50.135
Goodbye, ma'am.

00:24:50.219 --> 00:24:51.595
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:24:52.596 --> 00:24:53.639
[line disconnects]

00:24:53.722 --> 00:24:56.141
Was that a call from the chairwoman?

00:24:56.600 --> 00:24:58.435
-Yeah.
-[shrieks]

00:24:59.019 --> 00:25:00.354
[exclaims excitedly]

00:25:00.729 --> 00:25:02.689
-That startled me.
-[chuckles excitedly]

00:25:04.191 --> 00:25:05.609
That was such a surprise.

00:25:05.692 --> 00:25:07.194
[Wonseok vocalizing]

00:25:09.029 --> 00:25:10.948
I heard that the chairwoman
is getting discharged.

00:25:11.031 --> 00:25:13.408
-I wonder if she'll start work right away.
-[inhales sharply]

00:25:13.700 --> 00:25:15.536
I think that'd be a bit difficult

00:25:15.619 --> 00:25:17.871
since she'll need
to take it easy for a while.

00:25:17.955 --> 00:25:19.164
Also, considering her age.

00:25:19.248 --> 00:25:22.292
Then the acting chairman
will be Mr. Kim, right?

00:25:22.793 --> 00:25:24.169
Since Director Jang isn't here.

00:25:24.253 --> 00:25:25.838
[inhales sharply]

00:25:25.921 --> 00:25:27.047
That's probable.

00:25:27.131 --> 00:25:28.340
[sighs wearily]

00:25:28.423 --> 00:25:30.467
-Oh, no.
-Why?

00:25:30.801 --> 00:25:33.637
Don't you think I've been
a bit rude to Ms. Yoo recently?

00:25:34.429 --> 00:25:35.514
[exclaims]

00:25:35.597 --> 00:25:36.598
Perhaps...

00:25:37.808 --> 00:25:38.851
[sighs softly]

00:25:39.226 --> 00:25:40.978
-...just a little.
-[sighs]

00:25:41.061 --> 00:25:43.605
I bet I'm on her bad side now.

00:25:43.689 --> 00:25:47.234
[chuckles] If you are,
then what about Ms. Oh?

00:25:47.317 --> 00:25:48.652
-[chuckling]
-What about me?

00:25:48.735 --> 00:25:49.778
[both gasp]

00:25:50.404 --> 00:25:51.488
Nothing.

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:53.907
You must have a lot of free time, Sejung,

00:25:53.991 --> 00:25:55.659
worrying about such things.

00:25:56.243 --> 00:25:58.829
It's not like Ms. Yoo
is getting married right now.

00:25:58.912 --> 00:26:00.539
Focus on work.

00:26:03.333 --> 00:26:07.421
Also, you never really know with couples
until they walk down the aisle.

00:26:08.422 --> 00:26:09.840
Oh, good morning, Ms. Yoo.

00:26:09.923 --> 00:26:11.175
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:26:11.925 --> 00:26:13.218
[Ms. Oh chuckles softly]

00:26:14.094 --> 00:26:15.262
Here. [chuckles softly]

00:26:15.888 --> 00:26:17.055
[Wonseok] Thank you.

00:26:17.139 --> 00:26:18.765
You really didn't need to.

00:26:18.849 --> 00:26:20.017
Seriously.

00:26:20.100 --> 00:26:22.811
We should. It's give and take.

00:26:22.895 --> 00:26:23.896
[Ms. Oh] "Give and take"?

00:26:24.229 --> 00:26:25.355
We're a family, aren't we?

00:26:25.439 --> 00:26:26.773
You're upsetting me now.

00:26:28.233 --> 00:26:29.234
Come sit.

00:26:29.693 --> 00:26:30.777
Thank you.

00:26:35.365 --> 00:26:37.409
You heard that Chairwoman
has been discharged, right?

00:26:37.492 --> 00:26:39.328
-Yes.
-She's going to visit her soon.

00:26:39.661 --> 00:26:40.746
Is that so?

00:26:40.829 --> 00:26:42.039
[exclaiming thoughtfully]

00:26:42.122 --> 00:26:44.750
Then I should give you some advice.

00:26:45.792 --> 00:26:47.628
Are you good at omok?

00:26:48.170 --> 00:26:49.254
Omok?

00:26:49.796 --> 00:26:52.299
-A bit.
-She's really good at it.

00:26:52.382 --> 00:26:54.176
She even wins against the computer.

00:26:54.259 --> 00:26:56.345
-She's the Lee Sedol of omok.
-[exclaims dismissively]

00:26:56.428 --> 00:26:57.429
[Ms. Oh] Really?

00:26:57.512 --> 00:27:00.057
The chairwoman is also the queen of omok.

00:27:00.766 --> 00:27:02.100
She almost never loses.

00:27:02.768 --> 00:27:03.977
[exclaims in amazement]

00:27:04.061 --> 00:27:05.896
Then should I go play omok with her?

00:27:05.979 --> 00:27:07.522
[Ms. Oh] No.

00:27:07.940 --> 00:27:10.317
What will you do if you win against her?

00:27:11.485 --> 00:27:12.945
I think it was about ten years ago.

00:27:13.028 --> 00:27:15.739
A factory manager beat her once,

00:27:15.822 --> 00:27:17.532
and he had a rough week after that.

00:27:17.616 --> 00:27:20.327
She wouldn't even look him in the eye
for a whole week.

00:27:21.703 --> 00:27:23.622
He was totally out of her favor.

00:27:24.331 --> 00:27:26.625
Then, I shouldn't win.

00:27:26.708 --> 00:27:27.960
That's right.

00:27:28.043 --> 00:27:29.878
This is really important advice.

00:27:29.962 --> 00:27:31.588
No one would've told you but me.

00:27:32.005 --> 00:27:33.173
Thank you.

00:27:33.256 --> 00:27:35.133
Do you have any other advice?

00:27:35.217 --> 00:27:36.301
SAUNA

00:27:36.385 --> 00:27:38.178
-[sighs] Jinhwa.
-Yes?

00:27:38.261 --> 00:27:40.681
-What should we have for dinner?
-[hums thoughtfully]

00:27:40.764 --> 00:27:42.975
How about Szechuan-style
sweet and sour pork?

00:27:43.058 --> 00:27:45.811
I'll make it for you.
We just need to buy pork.

00:27:45.894 --> 00:27:49.356
Hey, look at you all excited
about the cooking school these days.

00:27:49.439 --> 00:27:52.859
I think that's where my hidden talent is.

00:27:52.943 --> 00:27:53.986
[imitates knife chopping]

00:27:54.069 --> 00:27:55.195
-[exclaims]
-[chuckles]

00:27:55.278 --> 00:27:57.823
[chuckles] I can't even be bothered
to shop for groceries.

00:27:57.906 --> 00:27:58.991
Let's just eat out.

00:27:59.074 --> 00:28:00.742
Call Wooju out.

00:28:00.826 --> 00:28:03.745
Geez, I was going to show off my skills.

00:28:05.580 --> 00:28:06.707
[exclaims quizzically]

00:28:06.790 --> 00:28:07.833
Mom.

00:28:08.959 --> 00:28:10.043
Isn't that Wooju?

00:28:10.752 --> 00:28:12.504
[Eunsook] Hey, it is.

00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:14.631
That's a woman in front of him.

00:28:15.549 --> 00:28:16.591
Who is that?

00:28:18.635 --> 00:28:21.013
I'm Lee Soyeong,
a reporter from Junghan Magazine.

00:28:21.096 --> 00:28:23.432
I saw that you
canceled the press conference.

00:28:23.515 --> 00:28:25.684
Could you tell me about it?

00:28:26.393 --> 00:28:28.645
[chief officer] The moment
our department store is mentioned,

00:28:28.729 --> 00:28:30.897
we'll estimate the business loss
caused by defamation

00:28:30.981 --> 00:28:32.149
and file a claim for damages.

00:28:32.232 --> 00:28:33.275
[gulps]

00:28:33.483 --> 00:28:34.484
It's nothing.

00:28:34.568 --> 00:28:36.194
I had it all wrong.

00:28:37.362 --> 00:28:40.157
I'm sorry for all the trouble I've caused.

00:28:48.957 --> 00:28:49.958
[Soyeong] Excuse me.

00:28:50.417 --> 00:28:51.418
Please wait.

00:28:52.377 --> 00:28:53.920
If you called for a press conference,

00:28:54.004 --> 00:28:55.630
you must've had some kind of proof

00:28:55.714 --> 00:28:57.674
that the Myungsoondang's heir
committed fraud.

00:28:59.134 --> 00:29:01.136
I'd prefer it
if you stopped asking me about it.

00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:04.181
Excuse me.

00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:06.141
Here.

00:29:07.059 --> 00:29:09.770
If you ever change your mind,
please call me.

00:29:18.487 --> 00:29:19.529
[Wooju sighs softly]

00:29:21.823 --> 00:29:22.991
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:29:23.075 --> 00:29:24.451
[Eunsook] A press conference?

00:29:25.035 --> 00:29:26.912
Who is the heir of Myungsoondang?

00:29:28.038 --> 00:29:29.372
Do you know him?

00:29:29.456 --> 00:29:31.124
No, how would I know someone like that?

00:29:32.125 --> 00:29:33.418
The reporter came to me by mistake.

00:29:33.502 --> 00:29:34.836
Tell me now.

00:29:34.920 --> 00:29:35.921
Tell us.

00:29:36.004 --> 00:29:38.715
Otherwise, I'm going to ask her directly.

00:29:47.099 --> 00:29:49.184
[Jinhwa] Myungsoondang's Kim Wooju...

00:29:49.976 --> 00:29:50.977
[gasps]

00:29:51.853 --> 00:29:53.105
That's right.

00:29:53.188 --> 00:29:54.773
This is the guy.

00:29:54.856 --> 00:29:56.608
He was in Wooju's hospital room.

00:29:57.150 --> 00:29:58.318
And at that store, too.

00:29:58.401 --> 00:29:59.986
We saw him there with Meri.

00:30:00.070 --> 00:30:01.947
-[gasps]
-It's him, right?

00:30:04.074 --> 00:30:05.075
Oh, my.

00:30:05.575 --> 00:30:06.910
Oh, my gosh.

00:30:06.993 --> 00:30:09.621
-[sighs]
-Meri really hit the jackpot.

00:30:09.704 --> 00:30:11.873
How is she marrying
into such a rich family?

00:30:12.332 --> 00:30:13.500
But seriously,

00:30:14.084 --> 00:30:16.044
look at this guy.

00:30:16.128 --> 00:30:18.380
He looks so classy.

00:30:18.880 --> 00:30:22.175
Mom, I'm more envious
of how handsome he is

00:30:22.259 --> 00:30:23.802
than the fact that she's marrying rich.

00:30:23.885 --> 00:30:25.011
Oh, I could just...

00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:28.140
[softly] You startled me.

00:30:28.223 --> 00:30:29.432
[laughing]

00:30:32.561 --> 00:30:34.855
This is unbelievable.

00:30:36.189 --> 00:30:37.607
-Hey.
-Yeah?

00:30:37.691 --> 00:30:38.692
His family

00:30:39.401 --> 00:30:40.944
is from Myungsoondang, right?

00:30:44.364 --> 00:30:48.451
You already seem happy at the thought
of getting a granddaughter-in-law.

00:30:48.535 --> 00:30:51.163
I'm just happy to get rid of Wooju.

00:30:51.246 --> 00:30:52.622
[chuckles softly]

00:30:53.165 --> 00:30:54.416
Still, it's a relief

00:30:54.791 --> 00:30:57.294
that I get to see him
getting married before I die.

00:30:58.628 --> 00:31:00.839
Perhaps that's why Wooju's dad woke me up.

00:31:03.508 --> 00:31:05.385
You should live to see
your great-grandchild.

00:31:06.344 --> 00:31:07.888
Don't say that.

00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:10.682
What if they ask me to babysit?

00:31:11.266 --> 00:31:14.978
I'm old-fashioned, so I can't pamper kids
the way moms do these days.

00:31:15.228 --> 00:31:16.521
[chuckles]

00:31:17.564 --> 00:31:19.024
You look beautiful today, as always.

00:31:19.107 --> 00:31:20.233
[both chuckle]

00:31:20.984 --> 00:31:22.944
There's still time, please rest a bit.

00:31:23.028 --> 00:31:24.070
[chuckles softly]

00:31:28.909 --> 00:31:31.036
Because you told me not to,

00:31:31.119 --> 00:31:34.497
I haven't looked
into Ms. Yoo Meri's personal background.

00:31:35.290 --> 00:31:36.374
But...

00:31:38.376 --> 00:31:39.794
are you sure about this?

00:31:41.129 --> 00:31:43.048
I met her a couple of times.

00:31:43.131 --> 00:31:44.674
She seemed like a good person.

00:31:45.550 --> 00:31:46.843
I haven't lost my touch yet.

00:31:48.178 --> 00:31:49.554
Yes, ma'am. [chuckles softly]

00:31:50.013 --> 00:31:51.514
Ask them where they are.

00:31:51.598 --> 00:31:52.766
Yes, ma'am.

00:31:57.312 --> 00:31:58.396
[sighs softly]

00:31:58.480 --> 00:31:59.481
Yes.

00:32:00.315 --> 00:32:02.275
We're at the flower shop
in front of the house.

00:32:03.193 --> 00:32:04.361
We'll be there soon.

00:32:04.694 --> 00:32:05.695
Okay.

00:32:05.987 --> 00:32:07.030
[line disconnects]

00:32:07.113 --> 00:32:10.033
I think Grandma is in a hurry to meet you.

00:32:10.116 --> 00:32:11.243
Do I look okay today?

00:32:11.785 --> 00:32:12.827
You look beautiful.

00:32:12.911 --> 00:32:14.746
Let's go. [giggles]

00:32:16.915 --> 00:32:18.541
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

00:32:31.888 --> 00:32:33.390
[doorbell chiming]

00:32:36.476 --> 00:32:37.936
[doorbell chiming]

00:32:38.520 --> 00:32:39.646
That must be them.

00:32:40.105 --> 00:32:42.065
-Okay, I'll go and let them in.
-Sure.

00:32:44.109 --> 00:32:45.568
[Eunsook gasps in awe]

00:32:52.701 --> 00:32:55.078
Mom, this house is... [scoffs]

00:32:55.161 --> 00:32:57.122
You said you had something to tell me

00:32:58.206 --> 00:32:59.749
about Ms. Yoo Meri.

00:33:00.125 --> 00:33:01.126
I do.

00:33:01.918 --> 00:33:03.545
Let me introduce myself first.

00:33:04.963 --> 00:33:05.964
I am

00:33:06.589 --> 00:33:11.761
the ex-mother-in-law of Meri,
who is currently dating your grandson.

00:33:11.845 --> 00:33:13.096
And I'm her ex-sister-in-law.

00:33:13.888 --> 00:33:14.889
Mother-in-law?

00:33:16.349 --> 00:33:17.350
Don't tell me...

00:33:17.809 --> 00:33:19.853
Didn't you know she's a divorcée?

00:33:19.936 --> 00:33:21.479
[♪ tense music playing]

00:33:21.563 --> 00:33:22.564
See?

00:33:22.647 --> 00:33:24.858
She was about to ruin another man's life.

00:33:25.483 --> 00:33:26.484
Gosh.

00:33:26.901 --> 00:33:29.988
Please, take your time
and tell me what you mean.

00:33:30.071 --> 00:33:31.239
Yes, ma'am.

00:33:31.323 --> 00:33:33.742
-That girl, Meri...
-That girl...

00:33:44.002 --> 00:33:45.337
[phone vibrating]

00:33:46.963 --> 00:33:47.964
Yes, we've arrived.

00:33:49.591 --> 00:33:50.592
Pardon?

00:33:50.675 --> 00:33:52.927
She asked to see you alone.

00:33:55.221 --> 00:33:57.140
What? All of a sudden...

00:34:00.727 --> 00:34:01.895
Oh, okay.

00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:04.481
I'm sorry.

00:34:04.564 --> 00:34:06.566
I don't think you can meet Grandma today.

00:34:06.649 --> 00:34:09.194
She says she's suddenly not feeling well.

00:34:09.277 --> 00:34:10.695
Oh, really?

00:34:10.779 --> 00:34:12.489
Is she very sick?

00:34:12.572 --> 00:34:14.366
Well, I'm not so sure.

00:34:14.991 --> 00:34:16.534
I'll have to go see her.

00:34:16.618 --> 00:34:18.453
Do you mind waiting in the car?

00:34:18.536 --> 00:34:21.164
No, don't worry about me, and go in.

00:34:24.376 --> 00:34:25.377
Go on.

00:34:40.225 --> 00:34:41.226
I'll get going.

00:34:49.401 --> 00:34:51.653
[door opens, closes]

00:34:52.987 --> 00:34:53.988
What's...

00:34:54.072 --> 00:34:55.407
Is Ms. Yoo Meri

00:34:56.825 --> 00:34:57.826
divorced?

00:34:57.909 --> 00:34:59.327
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

00:35:03.373 --> 00:35:04.666
[Kim Wooju clears throat]

00:35:04.749 --> 00:35:07.627
We were going to tell you about that
along with everything else.

00:35:07.711 --> 00:35:08.878
"Everything else"?

00:35:10.213 --> 00:35:12.799
I guess there's more
that I'd be surprised about.

00:35:30.734 --> 00:35:32.485
[♪ soft, poignant music playing]

00:35:33.319 --> 00:35:34.612
Meri... [breath trembling]

00:35:35.321 --> 00:35:37.198
Can I ask you to think over this again?

00:35:37.282 --> 00:35:38.950
I don't have any money.

00:35:39.033 --> 00:35:41.578
[crying] Could you please talk to Beauté

00:35:42.787 --> 00:35:44.789
and ask them to drop the lawsuit?

00:35:44.873 --> 00:35:47.208
Why did you have to take things this far?

00:35:47.292 --> 00:35:49.461
What made you take it this far?

00:35:52.380 --> 00:35:55.592
Seeing you broken
and falling apart like this

00:35:55.675 --> 00:35:57.177
doesn't make me happy

00:35:58.678 --> 00:35:59.721
or satisfied.

00:35:59.804 --> 00:36:00.847
[sobbing]

00:36:03.016 --> 00:36:05.477
Let's forget that you hurt me

00:36:06.686 --> 00:36:08.313
and your hatred toward me.

00:36:09.439 --> 00:36:11.357
Let's forget it all...

00:36:12.192 --> 00:36:14.402
and just keep the good memories.

00:36:14.944 --> 00:36:16.070
[sighs softly]

00:36:18.281 --> 00:36:19.866
Maybe I'm being punished.

00:36:23.703 --> 00:36:26.790
All the good days are behind me...

00:36:29.501 --> 00:36:31.544
and I lost a good woman like Meri.

00:36:34.005 --> 00:36:35.131
[chuckles wistfully]

00:36:36.174 --> 00:36:37.926
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

00:36:58.780 --> 00:36:59.781
Meri,

00:37:00.782 --> 00:37:01.783
I'm sorry.

00:37:06.788 --> 00:37:07.956
I know it's late,

00:37:10.208 --> 00:37:11.334
but I really mean it.

00:37:12.252 --> 00:37:13.419
I'm really sorry.

00:37:21.135 --> 00:37:23.054
I want you to be happy, too.

00:37:25.306 --> 00:37:26.307
SISTER

00:37:28.434 --> 00:37:29.435
[sighs wearily]

00:37:32.146 --> 00:37:33.147
What?

00:37:36.317 --> 00:37:37.443
What am I doing?

00:37:39.445 --> 00:37:40.446
Meri?

00:37:42.031 --> 00:37:43.741
Why would she call me?

00:37:47.495 --> 00:37:48.496
What?

00:37:49.122 --> 00:37:50.206
You went where?

00:37:50.790 --> 00:37:51.958
[breath trembling]

00:37:52.667 --> 00:37:54.043
Why would you do that?

00:37:54.544 --> 00:37:56.462
Stop it already.

00:37:56.546 --> 00:38:00.133
[yelling] You and Mom both,
please stop it already!

00:38:00.300 --> 00:38:02.468
-[line disconnects]
-[sobbing] Oh, gosh...

00:38:08.892 --> 00:38:11.477
CEO YOO MERI

00:38:13.479 --> 00:38:14.564
[mouse clicks]

00:38:15.773 --> 00:38:16.774
[phone pings]

00:38:19.319 --> 00:38:20.653
KIM WOOJU

00:38:20.737 --> 00:38:21.821
[Wooju] Meri.

00:38:21.905 --> 00:38:24.616
It looks like my mom
went to see Mr. Kim's grandma.

00:38:24.699 --> 00:38:26.367
I think she said some things about you.

00:38:26.451 --> 00:38:27.785
I'm really sorry.

00:38:27.869 --> 00:38:28.912
I apologize on her behalf.

00:38:30.872 --> 00:38:32.582
[♪ melancholy music playing]

00:38:32.957 --> 00:38:34.083
I'm sorry.

00:38:34.167 --> 00:38:35.752
I don't think you can meet Grandma today.

00:38:35.835 --> 00:38:38.129
She says she's suddenly not feeling well.

00:38:39.047 --> 00:38:40.298
[sighs wearily]

00:38:41.466 --> 00:38:43.051
So, that's what happened.

00:38:48.056 --> 00:38:49.140
[sighs softly]

00:38:59.317 --> 00:39:00.318
[Philnyun] What?

00:39:00.401 --> 00:39:02.111
She even committed fraud?

00:39:06.032 --> 00:39:07.241
[phone vibrating]

00:39:10.495 --> 00:39:12.538
MYUNGSOON

00:39:12.830 --> 00:39:13.915
[clears throat]

00:39:14.332 --> 00:39:15.917
-Hello.
-Hi.

00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:18.586
I was just wondering
how Chairwoman is doing.

00:39:19.295 --> 00:39:21.839
Oh, it wasn't something serious.

00:39:21.923 --> 00:39:24.050
She said she was
just not feeling her best.

00:39:24.759 --> 00:39:25.760
I see.

00:39:26.511 --> 00:39:29.013
Didn't she say anything else?

00:39:30.056 --> 00:39:31.057
No.

00:39:32.976 --> 00:39:34.102
Did you get home safely?

00:39:34.769 --> 00:39:36.104
I'm on my way now.

00:39:36.771 --> 00:39:40.525
I'll rearrange the meeting
for some other time when there's a chance.

00:39:41.192 --> 00:39:42.527
-For the time being...
-About that.

00:39:42.610 --> 00:39:44.320
Don't worry about it too much.

00:39:44.404 --> 00:39:45.863
It's not urgent.

00:39:46.823 --> 00:39:47.824
Yes.

00:39:49.283 --> 00:39:50.493
Good night.

00:39:52.662 --> 00:39:53.663
[line disconnects]

00:39:58.584 --> 00:39:59.836
[sighs wearily]

00:40:10.680 --> 00:40:11.848
[sighs wearily]

00:40:17.103 --> 00:40:18.271
[phone vibrating]

00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:20.690
MOM

00:40:24.861 --> 00:40:26.195
No, that one.

00:40:26.279 --> 00:40:28.406
-They're all the same.
-Mom.

00:40:28.489 --> 00:40:29.574
Hey, sweetie.

00:40:30.408 --> 00:40:34.162
Didn't you say that you were
going to meet his grandma?

00:40:34.245 --> 00:40:37.373
Why didn't you call
to tell me how it went?

00:40:37.457 --> 00:40:39.500
I've been waiting forever.

00:40:40.710 --> 00:40:43.421
-[whispering indistinctly]
-[exclaims]

00:40:45.089 --> 00:40:46.090
You didn't meet her?

00:40:48.051 --> 00:40:49.886
[sighs softly] Well...

00:40:52.013 --> 00:40:53.264
What?

00:40:57.810 --> 00:41:00.396
Mom, are you sure about this?

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:01.481
My gosh.

00:41:02.106 --> 00:41:03.149
It doesn't matter

00:41:03.566 --> 00:41:06.611
whether I'm sure or not, okay?

00:41:08.905 --> 00:41:11.240
I'm going to settle this once and for all.

00:41:12.200 --> 00:41:13.868
Okay, I get it. [in English] Calm down.

00:41:14.243 --> 00:41:15.536
Calm down.

00:41:15.620 --> 00:41:16.621
[breathing heavily]

00:41:18.456 --> 00:41:19.957
[in Korean] Mom, isn't that them?

00:41:20.041 --> 00:41:21.209
-Where?
-There.

00:41:21.292 --> 00:41:23.461
[gasps] Gosh, yes.

00:41:23.795 --> 00:41:25.838
Right, wait a minute.

00:41:25.922 --> 00:41:26.923
Wait.

00:41:27.507 --> 00:41:29.467
-[in English] Stop. [grunts]
-[tires screech]

00:41:32.345 --> 00:41:33.513
[in Korean] Hey!

00:41:33.596 --> 00:41:35.264
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

00:41:37.517 --> 00:41:39.143
Oh, my gosh. Who are you?

00:41:39.227 --> 00:41:41.521
Oh, my. [stutters] Meri's mother!

00:41:41.604 --> 00:41:44.732
-Let's end this together!
-No, stop!

00:41:44.816 --> 00:41:46.609
I'll make you pay for everything

00:41:46.692 --> 00:41:49.695
-Ms. Oh!
-you did to my daughter!

00:41:49.779 --> 00:41:52.615
What's happening? Jinhwa!

00:41:52.698 --> 00:41:55.034
-Let's end this together!
-Ms. Oh!

00:41:55.326 --> 00:41:59.413
I'm going to make you pay
for what you did to my daughter!

00:41:59.497 --> 00:42:01.415
-Why are you...
-Ms. Oh!

00:42:01.499 --> 00:42:02.959
[Jinhwa] Stop this!

00:42:03.709 --> 00:42:07.130
-[screams] Hey!
-How dare you mess with my sister?

00:42:07.213 --> 00:42:09.715
-Who's this? Let me go.
-How dare you?

00:42:11.259 --> 00:42:12.260
Hey!

00:42:12.343 --> 00:42:13.344
[screams]

00:42:15.513 --> 00:42:16.973
[all screaming, grunting]

00:42:20.059 --> 00:42:21.853
[Eunsook] Please, help.

00:42:21.936 --> 00:42:24.230
-[Youngsook] To my daughter...
-Please, help me.

00:42:24.313 --> 00:42:25.523
-Ms. Oh!
-You're so dead.

00:42:27.024 --> 00:42:29.944
[Jinhwa] Please, help me!

00:42:48.921 --> 00:42:50.131
[sighs wearily]

00:42:57.096 --> 00:42:58.264
You're here early.

00:42:59.098 --> 00:43:00.099
[exclaims quizzically]

00:43:00.766 --> 00:43:01.851
What?

00:43:01.934 --> 00:43:03.394
Isn't today your trial?

00:43:03.477 --> 00:43:04.478
[chuckles softly]

00:43:04.896 --> 00:43:09.275
I came in case you were upset
about a guy standing you up again.

00:43:09.358 --> 00:43:10.359
What?

00:43:11.235 --> 00:43:12.236
What is it?

00:43:12.320 --> 00:43:15.781
Do you think I'm drowning my sorrows
because a guy stood me up?

00:43:15.865 --> 00:43:16.908
I'm not.

00:43:19.702 --> 00:43:21.329
Are you trying to flirt with me?

00:43:21.412 --> 00:43:23.080
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

00:43:24.373 --> 00:43:26.292
Are you trying to flirt with me?

00:43:28.044 --> 00:43:29.128
[sighs deeply]

00:43:31.047 --> 00:43:33.132
Someone comforted me recently.

00:43:34.383 --> 00:43:38.095
I realized that money
isn't everything in this world.

00:43:39.180 --> 00:43:40.306
Thanks to that person,

00:43:40.932 --> 00:43:42.975
I feel so much at ease now.

00:43:43.726 --> 00:43:46.145
I'm not sure who that person is,

00:43:46.229 --> 00:43:48.689
but they must be a really great person.

00:43:50.149 --> 00:43:52.026
Anyway, I like your attitude now.

00:43:52.735 --> 00:43:53.736
[in English] Respect.

00:43:55.488 --> 00:43:56.489
[in English] Respect

00:43:57.448 --> 00:43:58.824
[both chuckle]

00:44:04.872 --> 00:44:05.957
[in Korean] Your trial...

00:44:06.749 --> 00:44:08.209
I hope it goes well.

00:44:18.261 --> 00:44:19.553
[in Korean] I'll get going first.

00:44:23.391 --> 00:44:24.725
Wait for me!

00:44:24.809 --> 00:44:26.185
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

00:44:32.858 --> 00:44:36.112
By the way,
why did you ask me for such a favor?

00:44:36.946 --> 00:44:38.447
Because I had no one to ask.

00:44:38.531 --> 00:44:40.574
Wait, is that really it?

00:44:43.077 --> 00:44:44.245
You can say no.

00:44:44.328 --> 00:44:46.163
That's not what I'm saying.

00:44:46.247 --> 00:44:47.957
I'm just curious.

00:44:48.040 --> 00:44:49.417
Like, when do I start?

00:44:49.500 --> 00:44:52.044
This comes with a lot
of responsibility, doesn't it?

00:44:52.670 --> 00:44:54.005
Wait for me!

00:44:54.088 --> 00:44:55.423
[Sanghyeon] Hurry up!

00:44:55.506 --> 00:44:57.174
[Jingyeong] Oh, seriously.

00:44:57.258 --> 00:44:58.509
You're too fast.

00:45:01.762 --> 00:45:03.347
[♪ soft jazz music playing in background]

00:45:04.515 --> 00:45:07.685
[Meri] We thought everything
would go smoothly,

00:45:08.811 --> 00:45:12.523
but as we each carried
our own unspoken worries,

00:45:13.024 --> 00:45:16.277
life got busier, and we drifted apart.

00:45:21.032 --> 00:45:23.409
Did I tell you
that Eungsoo quit the company?

00:45:23.826 --> 00:45:25.244
No, you mean Mr. Jang?

00:45:26.662 --> 00:45:29.206
He suddenly wants to become
an esports team owner.

00:45:29.290 --> 00:45:32.710
He wanted to chase his passion,
so he handed in his resignation last week.

00:45:33.085 --> 00:45:34.086
I see.

00:45:34.170 --> 00:45:36.297
-I didn't know he liked games.
-He does.

00:45:36.672 --> 00:45:40.301
He's busy these days
scouting professional gamers.

00:45:40.384 --> 00:45:43.012
And it makes me busy, too,
trying to fill in for him.

00:45:49.393 --> 00:45:52.730
You also seemed busy,
seeing how you call less.

00:45:53.481 --> 00:45:54.523
[hesitates]

00:45:54.607 --> 00:45:56.525
It's because of the meetings.

00:45:57.193 --> 00:45:58.736
With the new project,

00:45:58.819 --> 00:46:01.906
it's been a bit hectic
going back and forth from Daejeon.

00:46:01.989 --> 00:46:04.408
Oh, I see.

00:46:09.622 --> 00:46:11.791
MADAM KO

00:46:15.252 --> 00:46:16.420
[phone vibrating]

00:46:16.921 --> 00:46:18.339
Can you give me a minute?

00:46:43.697 --> 00:46:45.366
I'd like to pay, please.

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:52.123
[card reader beeps]

00:46:52.206 --> 00:46:54.125
Please sign here.

00:46:57.002 --> 00:46:58.295
-[printer whirring]
-[receipt rips]

00:46:59.713 --> 00:47:01.382
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:47:02.591 --> 00:47:05.261
[Kim Wooju] No, I told you already.

00:47:05.344 --> 00:47:08.597
Unlike how you think...

00:47:09.223 --> 00:47:10.474
No, I mean...

00:47:11.725 --> 00:47:12.726
[sighs wearily]

00:47:13.686 --> 00:47:16.063
Grandma, can you please reconsider?

00:47:17.565 --> 00:47:19.525
[♪ melancholy music playing]

00:47:26.449 --> 00:47:28.367
I'm sorry. I have to get home.

00:47:28.451 --> 00:47:30.578
It's fine. Your grandma is asking for you.

00:47:30.661 --> 00:47:31.871
You should get going.

00:47:32.246 --> 00:47:33.414
[engine starts]

00:48:19.251 --> 00:48:20.794
Since everyone is here,

00:48:22.713 --> 00:48:24.131
I'll tell you my decisions.

00:48:26.342 --> 00:48:28.219
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

00:48:39.563 --> 00:48:40.731
[sighs softly]

00:48:42.233 --> 00:48:44.860
Grandma, can you please reconsider?

00:48:45.486 --> 00:48:47.196
[sighs wearily] No, I mean...

00:48:48.280 --> 00:48:49.490
[phone vibrating]

00:48:53.953 --> 00:48:55.496
MYUNGSIK

00:48:58.082 --> 00:48:59.083
Hi.

00:48:59.625 --> 00:49:00.626
[Kim Wooju] Where are you?

00:49:02.211 --> 00:49:04.004
I'm at the playground
in front of my house.

00:49:04.630 --> 00:49:07.591
I came out for fresh air
since the wind is nice.

00:49:07.675 --> 00:49:08.884
"Came out for fresh air"?

00:49:08.968 --> 00:49:10.511
I bet you were out this whole time.

00:49:10.970 --> 00:49:11.971
Pardon?

00:49:12.054 --> 00:49:14.974
You haven't even changed.
What are you doing all alone at this hour?

00:49:25.609 --> 00:49:26.652
[line disconnects]

00:49:27.319 --> 00:49:28.404
Wooju.

00:49:35.619 --> 00:49:38.581
I was on my way to your place to see you.

00:49:38.664 --> 00:49:41.792
And I saw you just sitting here,

00:49:41.875 --> 00:49:44.253
glowing under the lights
with that stunning beauty.

00:49:45.921 --> 00:49:47.673
What did your grandma say?

00:49:49.091 --> 00:49:52.052
I'm sure she called you in
because she had something to say.

00:49:52.136 --> 00:49:53.178
[hesitates]

00:49:55.097 --> 00:49:56.181
[clears throat]

00:49:57.766 --> 00:49:59.518
She's against us, right?

00:50:00.102 --> 00:50:01.103
What?

00:50:01.186 --> 00:50:04.356
Wooju's mom paid a visit to your grandma.

00:50:05.733 --> 00:50:07.651
I think I know what she told her.

00:50:10.946 --> 00:50:12.823
I'm fine,

00:50:12.906 --> 00:50:14.867
so don't struggle in between.

00:50:15.159 --> 00:50:16.535
I'm not struggling.

00:50:18.245 --> 00:50:19.496
I heard you

00:50:20.039 --> 00:50:22.249
talking to your grandma at the restaurant.

00:50:24.418 --> 00:50:25.711
[exclaims in realization]

00:50:26.378 --> 00:50:27.504
[sighs wearily]

00:50:27.588 --> 00:50:30.257
Grandma, can you please reconsider?

00:50:33.344 --> 00:50:36.930
[chuckles softly]
I'm very grateful for the offer,

00:50:37.014 --> 00:50:39.892
but I'm not ready
to take over the company yet.

00:50:40.643 --> 00:50:43.187
How about we hire a professional manager?

00:50:43.854 --> 00:50:45.356
You should've stayed to hear the rest.

00:50:45.773 --> 00:50:49.526
Grandma wants me to take over the company.

00:50:49.610 --> 00:50:51.278
-What?
-Geez.

00:50:51.362 --> 00:50:52.821
You went off in your own head again.

00:50:54.740 --> 00:50:58.369
Well, she didn't ask
to see me again, so...

00:50:58.452 --> 00:51:01.288
About that, she said
she needs a bit more time.

00:51:02.122 --> 00:51:03.165
[acknowledges]

00:51:03.916 --> 00:51:04.917
What?

00:51:05.626 --> 00:51:07.211
She even committed fraud?

00:51:07.294 --> 00:51:10.172
But you said it yourself,

00:51:10.255 --> 00:51:11.924
anyone can make mistakes.

00:51:12.341 --> 00:51:15.094
What matters is having the heart
and the will to make things right.

00:51:15.844 --> 00:51:16.929
[sighs in exasperation]

00:51:18.555 --> 00:51:19.598
Grandma...

00:51:19.682 --> 00:51:20.766
I have a headache.

00:51:21.558 --> 00:51:22.935
Let me think about it.

00:51:24.520 --> 00:51:27.189
[Kim Wooju] Do you know how anxious
I've been, waiting for her permission?

00:51:27.648 --> 00:51:28.649
[sighs softly]

00:51:29.108 --> 00:51:30.984
You should've told me.

00:51:31.360 --> 00:51:32.444
[chuckles softly]

00:51:33.445 --> 00:51:35.030
Do you know why she called me in today?

00:51:42.621 --> 00:51:43.831
She gave me this.

00:51:45.249 --> 00:51:47.209
She said, you can earn money whenever,

00:51:47.292 --> 00:51:49.294
eat delicious food whenever,

00:51:49.837 --> 00:51:51.714
and travel whenever.

00:51:53.924 --> 00:51:55.634
But there's a time for a proposal.

00:51:58.095 --> 00:52:01.140
She also said, if I ever meet someone
I want to spend the rest of my life with,

00:52:01.223 --> 00:52:02.766
I shouldn't lose her.

00:52:02.850 --> 00:52:04.518
[♪ gentle, dreamy music playing]

00:52:20.993 --> 00:52:21.994
Meri.

00:52:25.789 --> 00:52:27.833
Would you marry me?

00:52:35.132 --> 00:52:37.176
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

00:52:44.057 --> 00:52:45.058
Meri?

00:52:45.726 --> 00:52:46.727
Yes.

00:52:46.810 --> 00:52:48.061
[chuckles in relief]

00:52:49.229 --> 00:52:50.355
[chuckles softly]

00:52:51.523 --> 00:52:52.691
[clears throat] Well,

00:52:53.358 --> 00:52:56.111
someone said I shouldn't answer too fast.

00:52:57.488 --> 00:52:59.990
[chuckling] I was counting to ten,
but I failed.

00:53:01.074 --> 00:53:02.451
-[chuckles]
-[Meri sniffles]

00:53:18.425 --> 00:53:20.636
-[sniffles]
-[sighs contentedly]

00:53:50.082 --> 00:53:51.250
[sighs contentedly]

00:53:56.255 --> 00:53:57.589
[birds chirping]

00:54:07.349 --> 00:54:09.685
I've made many mistakes,

00:54:09.768 --> 00:54:12.771
but thank you
for forgiving me and accepting me.

00:54:12.855 --> 00:54:14.106
Sure.

00:54:14.189 --> 00:54:16.483
I hope you learned a lot from this.

00:54:17.651 --> 00:54:19.403
Make sure to keep it in your mind.

00:54:20.529 --> 00:54:21.697
I'll keep it in mind.

00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:23.407
I will, too.

00:54:23.490 --> 00:54:24.950
Mom! [chuckles]

00:54:25.742 --> 00:54:27.369
I heard Wooju's fiancée is coming.

00:54:27.452 --> 00:54:29.246
Mom, look to your left.

00:54:29.830 --> 00:54:30.831
She's here.

00:54:30.914 --> 00:54:32.291
Nice to meet you, Ms. Kim.

00:54:32.374 --> 00:54:33.709
My name is Yoo Meri.

00:54:33.792 --> 00:54:34.793
Hi, I'm...

00:54:37.212 --> 00:54:38.338
Wooju's aunt.

00:54:38.964 --> 00:54:40.632
This is his cousin.

00:54:40.716 --> 00:54:41.800
Say hi.

00:54:41.884 --> 00:54:44.720
We already know each other.
Aren't I right?

00:54:44.803 --> 00:54:46.930
-Have you been well?
-Yes.

00:54:47.014 --> 00:54:48.765
[Eungsoo and Miyeon chuckle]

00:54:49.099 --> 00:54:50.183
[Miyeon] You know,

00:54:51.143 --> 00:54:53.562
she resembles her mother a lot.

00:54:53.645 --> 00:54:55.981
Yeah, she does. She also looks fierce.

00:54:56.064 --> 00:54:57.566
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:54:57.649 --> 00:54:59.860
Have you seen my mother?

00:54:59.943 --> 00:55:01.820
We visited Yeosu, actually.

00:55:01.903 --> 00:55:04.865
We went there ourselves
on Grandma's order.

00:55:04.948 --> 00:55:06.241
It was quite far.

00:55:06.825 --> 00:55:08.368
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

00:55:10.329 --> 00:55:14.124
YOUNGSOOK'S RESTAURANT

00:55:25.177 --> 00:55:28.263
[exclaims contentedly]
How about this rolled omelet?

00:55:28.680 --> 00:55:29.806
Oh, my.

00:55:29.890 --> 00:55:30.891
[chuckles]

00:55:32.809 --> 00:55:35.145
[Eungsoo slurping loudly,
hums in satisfaction]

00:55:36.355 --> 00:55:38.273
This place is delicious.

00:55:39.358 --> 00:55:40.692
Mom, try it.

00:55:40.776 --> 00:55:42.486
-[Miyeon] Stop eating.
-[Eungsoo] Just try it.

00:55:42.569 --> 00:55:44.655
Just put it in your mouth.

00:55:44.738 --> 00:55:46.823
-[Eungsoo] Okay.
-You must be from Seoul.

00:55:47.783 --> 00:55:49.951
How did you know?

00:55:50.035 --> 00:55:51.578
You're not using dialect.

00:55:51.662 --> 00:55:53.330
I see. [chuckles softly]

00:55:54.665 --> 00:55:55.832
Are you the owner?

00:55:55.916 --> 00:55:58.418
-What?
-How's the business?

00:55:59.044 --> 00:56:00.712
How much is the profit?

00:56:00.796 --> 00:56:02.381
How would I know?

00:56:02.464 --> 00:56:04.758
I'm just a kitchen assistant.

00:56:04.841 --> 00:56:06.677
She's the owner.

00:56:10.180 --> 00:56:11.973
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:56:14.059 --> 00:56:17.062
[Sunja] Geez, those were just testers.

00:56:17.145 --> 00:56:19.815
But he's making a meal out of it.

00:56:19.898 --> 00:56:21.900
If he eats like that
and doesn't buy anything,

00:56:21.983 --> 00:56:23.860
he's completely shameless.

00:56:24.361 --> 00:56:26.738
[clears throat] These... [chuckles]

00:56:26.822 --> 00:56:29.199
We're going to buy all of these.

00:56:29.282 --> 00:56:32.411
Could you pack these two up for us?

00:56:35.122 --> 00:56:37.624
[gasps] Oh, no.

00:56:37.708 --> 00:56:39.209
Wait.

00:56:39.751 --> 00:56:42.379
You can't take these, instead...

00:56:42.462 --> 00:56:44.464
Here, take this.

00:56:46.258 --> 00:56:49.386
Okay, then. But these cost the same,

00:56:49.970 --> 00:56:51.221
yet it's half the amount.

00:56:51.304 --> 00:56:53.682
Are you treating us differently
because we're not locals?

00:56:53.765 --> 00:56:56.601
-We're also in this business.
-It's not like that.

00:56:58.186 --> 00:57:01.189
-It's half the amount.
-Gosh, it's...

00:57:01.273 --> 00:57:03.358
-Hello.
-Oh, hey, Bohyeon.

00:57:03.442 --> 00:57:04.693
Wait a moment.

00:57:04.776 --> 00:57:06.069
Let's see.

00:57:06.153 --> 00:57:08.071
I packed all your favorites.

00:57:08.155 --> 00:57:09.489
Here.

00:57:09.573 --> 00:57:11.408
Enjoy it with your sister.

00:57:11.491 --> 00:57:13.034
Thank you.

00:57:20.333 --> 00:57:22.127
Thanks. Go on, now.

00:57:22.210 --> 00:57:23.712
Bye.

00:57:24.963 --> 00:57:27.716
[Sunja] Gosh, you're too generous.

00:57:27.799 --> 00:57:30.260
The business will fail at this rate.

00:57:30.343 --> 00:57:31.845
Nonsense.

00:57:32.512 --> 00:57:34.431
Oh, my. I'm sorry.

00:57:34.514 --> 00:57:37.893
Her mother died when she was younger,

00:57:37.976 --> 00:57:40.270
and her father's not home
as he's a fisherman.

00:57:40.353 --> 00:57:43.440
She's still a kid,
but she's got a younger one to look after.

00:57:43.523 --> 00:57:44.733
So, I feel bad for her.

00:57:44.816 --> 00:57:49.654
But she's too proud a girl
to take them for free.

00:57:49.738 --> 00:57:53.074
So, what else can I do
but give her a lot more?

00:57:53.158 --> 00:57:54.284
[chuckles]

00:57:54.534 --> 00:57:57.579
I'm not treating you differently,
so don't be upset.

00:57:57.662 --> 00:57:59.873
Oh, okay. [chuckles sheepishly]

00:57:59.956 --> 00:58:01.666
-So, you're from Seoul?
-Yes.

00:58:01.750 --> 00:58:04.711
Since you've been so gracious,
let's see...

00:58:05.337 --> 00:58:06.463
[grunts]

00:58:06.546 --> 00:58:07.798
Here.

00:58:07.881 --> 00:58:09.299
-Pollock pancakes?
-Pollock pancakes.

00:58:09.382 --> 00:58:11.134
-This is on the house.
-[chuckles]

00:58:11.218 --> 00:58:13.553
[chuckles] Our pollock pancakes
are amazing.

00:58:13.637 --> 00:58:14.763
[Eungsoo grunts]

00:58:16.181 --> 00:58:17.307
-[sighs]
-[grunts]

00:58:22.729 --> 00:58:23.772
[sighs softly]

00:58:25.565 --> 00:58:26.942
[line ringing]

00:58:27.692 --> 00:58:29.444
-[clears throat]
-Hi, Mom.

00:58:30.195 --> 00:58:32.906
I just saw Ms. Yoo Meri's mother,

00:58:32.989 --> 00:58:34.115
and I think...

00:58:35.116 --> 00:58:36.451
you'll like her.

00:58:36.535 --> 00:58:41.081
Like so, in relation to your marriage,
we played a very important role.

00:58:41.164 --> 00:58:42.666
-[laughs exultantly]
-[Miyeon chuckling]

00:58:44.376 --> 00:58:45.585
Thank you.

00:58:45.669 --> 00:58:49.089
Then I guess all that's left is
to set a date for the family meeting.

00:58:49.172 --> 00:58:51.091
About that...

00:58:52.133 --> 00:58:54.302
We're thinking of delaying our wedding.

00:58:55.720 --> 00:58:56.721
Why?

00:58:56.805 --> 00:58:59.641
Well, I just accepted the CEO position.

00:59:00.225 --> 00:59:02.853
So, I think it's only right
to focus more on the company right now.

00:59:03.728 --> 00:59:05.397
Meri also agreed to it.

00:59:06.064 --> 00:59:08.984
Yes, I also thought
that'd be for the best.

00:59:09.442 --> 00:59:10.443
[Philnyun] Is that right?

00:59:11.611 --> 00:59:14.114
If you both agree, then okay.

00:59:14.197 --> 00:59:15.574
I guess

00:59:16.449 --> 00:59:18.952
I'll just have to live longer.

00:59:19.035 --> 00:59:20.245
[all chuckle]

00:59:20.328 --> 00:59:22.122
[Miyeon] Oh, Mom...

00:59:22.956 --> 00:59:25.792
Son, this isn't the time for you to laugh.

00:59:25.876 --> 00:59:28.503
It's not too late yet.
How about I set you up?

00:59:28.587 --> 00:59:30.714
I'm a believer in natural encounters, Mom.

00:59:30.797 --> 00:59:33.049
I don't do blind dates, so no set-ups.

00:59:33.133 --> 00:59:34.551
It's not too late.

00:59:34.634 --> 00:59:37.012
Meri, do you have any friends
you can introduce?

00:59:37.095 --> 00:59:38.305
I have many.

00:59:38.388 --> 00:59:40.515
What do you think? Can you set him up?

00:59:40.599 --> 00:59:42.100
What kind of woman are you into?

00:59:42.183 --> 00:59:44.227
-Someone unlike Mom.
-[Miyeon] Someone like me.

00:59:45.395 --> 00:59:47.439
[Jingyeong] You guys are
going to live here from now on.

00:59:48.648 --> 00:59:51.276
This is also a place people stay in,

00:59:51.359 --> 00:59:53.111
so get used to it fast, okay?

00:59:54.029 --> 00:59:55.697
Especially you, Sweet.

00:59:56.406 --> 00:59:59.534
You've been looking so down lately,
just sleeping all the time.

01:00:01.453 --> 01:00:02.537
Or was it Sour?

01:00:04.497 --> 01:00:06.958
Oh, this is really confusing.

01:00:07.876 --> 01:00:09.419
Are you guys twins?

01:00:15.884 --> 01:00:19.054
How did your owner differentiate you two?

01:00:19.638 --> 01:00:21.139
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

01:00:22.682 --> 01:00:25.268
[sighs] Meal time.

01:00:46.498 --> 01:00:47.999
[sighs softly]

01:00:59.135 --> 01:01:00.637
[Jingyeong] Dear Mr. Baek.

01:01:01.179 --> 01:01:03.682
It's gotten quite cold
in the morning and at night.

01:01:03.765 --> 01:01:07.394
Winter must be near,
judging by the days also getting shorter.

01:01:08.144 --> 01:01:09.479
You're doing well, right?

01:01:10.063 --> 01:01:13.358
It's been all hospital and home for me,

01:01:13.441 --> 01:01:16.653
but lately, I've really been
enjoying raising the turtles.

01:01:16.736 --> 01:01:19.656
I can't even tell
a turtle from a terrapin,

01:01:19.739 --> 01:01:22.534
but I've been turning into a turtle expert

01:01:22.617 --> 01:01:24.786
from trying to tell
the twin-like Sweet and Sour apart,

01:01:25.537 --> 01:01:26.955
You said I just need to feed them

01:01:27.038 --> 01:01:29.624
and change their water from time to time.

01:01:29.708 --> 01:01:30.875
But guess what?

01:01:30.959 --> 01:01:32.836
I also have to check
if they're still alive

01:01:33.378 --> 01:01:36.047
because they're way too quiet.

01:01:37.298 --> 01:01:40.093
I think they're introverts,
taking after you.

01:01:40.176 --> 01:01:41.177
[chuckles]

01:01:44.597 --> 01:01:47.767
I'll be participating
in the Boston Marathon next spring.

01:01:47.851 --> 01:01:51.354
I'll complete it and send you
a proof photo at the Charles River.

01:01:51.438 --> 01:01:52.689
Would you like to join me

01:01:52.772 --> 01:01:54.774
for the next November's
New York City Marathon?

01:01:54.858 --> 01:01:56.901
I can complete the course now.

01:01:56.985 --> 01:02:01.114
If you want to match my pace,
you'll have to train hard until then.

01:02:01.197 --> 01:02:03.450
I'll take good care of your turtles,

01:02:03.533 --> 01:02:07.078
so don't worry and stay healthy.

01:02:07.162 --> 01:02:08.663
BEFORE I KNEW YOU,
I GOT ALONG WITHOUT POETRY

01:02:08.747 --> 01:02:11.583
Like these turtles,
who are dependent on their strong shells,

01:02:11.666 --> 01:02:15.712
I hope you're growing stronger
through your days there.

01:02:16.504 --> 01:02:17.839
I'll write to you again.

01:02:27.182 --> 01:02:28.558
[sighs deeply]

01:02:36.733 --> 01:02:38.526
1 YEAR LATER

01:02:38.610 --> 01:02:41.237
[Sejung] An outdoor wedding?
It looks like it's going to rain.

01:02:41.321 --> 01:02:42.489
[Ms. Oh] Tell me about it.

01:02:42.989 --> 01:02:44.616
Why do I have to carry things like this?

01:02:45.575 --> 01:02:47.827
What's wrong with it?
The grass smells nice.

01:02:47.911 --> 01:02:50.538
Also, I always dreamed
of having an outdoor wedding.

01:02:50.622 --> 01:02:51.998
He's right.

01:02:52.082 --> 01:02:54.417
And they say you live happily
if it rains on your wedding day.

01:02:54.501 --> 01:02:55.710
So, I guess it's lucky.

01:02:55.794 --> 01:02:56.836
How lucky!

01:02:56.920 --> 01:02:58.379
Whatever.

01:02:59.714 --> 01:03:00.715
[screams]

01:03:00.799 --> 01:03:02.050
[Wonseok] What's wrong?

01:03:02.509 --> 01:03:03.510
[Ms. Oh] Wait...

01:03:04.594 --> 01:03:05.595
What's this?

01:03:05.678 --> 01:03:08.181
I can't believe this. These are new!

01:03:08.890 --> 01:03:10.433
Oh, my clothes are new, too.

01:03:10.517 --> 01:03:11.810
[Wonseok] Me too.

01:03:11.893 --> 01:03:13.186
[Songhee] Oh, no...

01:03:13.269 --> 01:03:15.522
[Eungsoo] "Ms. Yoo Meri..."

01:03:15.605 --> 01:03:16.606
[Ms. Oh] My shoes...

01:03:16.689 --> 01:03:17.690
-Oh, hello.
-Hi.

01:03:17.774 --> 01:03:18.858
Oh, no. Are you hurt?

01:03:18.942 --> 01:03:20.527
No, it's just my heel.

01:03:20.610 --> 01:03:21.611
I see.

01:03:22.487 --> 01:03:24.614
-[Ms. Oh] No, not there.
-[Eungsoo] Let's see...

01:03:24.697 --> 01:03:28.243
"Thank you for attending today's..."

01:03:28.451 --> 01:03:30.995
[chuckles]
I heard your business is soaring.

01:03:31.079 --> 01:03:32.872
Oh, not at all.

01:03:32.956 --> 01:03:36.668
It went a bit viral on social media,

01:03:36.751 --> 01:03:40.004
and let's just say I don't have time
to go to the bathroom.

01:03:40.088 --> 01:03:42.132
-[customer 1] Thank you.
-[Sori] Thank you.

01:03:42.215 --> 01:03:44.300
Hello, what would you like?

01:03:44.384 --> 01:03:46.386
[customer 2] Can we get two packs
of green onion kimchi?

01:03:46.469 --> 01:03:48.138
-And two packs of seaweed stems, please.
-Okay.

01:03:48.221 --> 01:03:49.806
I heard the side dishes here
are really good.

01:03:49.889 --> 01:03:51.850
Really? Thank you.

01:03:51.933 --> 01:03:56.729
Gosh, thanks to Sori,
we went viral on social media.

01:03:56.813 --> 01:03:59.440
I don't even have time
to go to the bathroom.

01:03:59.524 --> 01:04:01.651
You could be buying a building soon.

01:04:01.734 --> 01:04:03.945
-Why not? Let me buy a building.
-[chuckling]

01:04:04.028 --> 01:04:05.363
-Hello.
-Hi.

01:04:05.446 --> 01:04:06.823
[in English] What is this one?

01:04:06.906 --> 01:04:08.908
[in English] It's made
by mixing dried radish

01:04:08.992 --> 01:04:12.871
with seasonings such as
red pepper powder and soy sauce.

01:04:12.954 --> 01:04:13.955
I see.

01:04:14.038 --> 01:04:15.582
-Can I try?
-Yes.

01:04:15.665 --> 01:04:17.167
-Thank you.
-Yes, of course.

01:04:17.250 --> 01:04:18.501
-Here.
-Thank you.

01:04:19.335 --> 01:04:22.755
We have more stuff inside,
so please do take a look.

01:04:22.839 --> 01:04:24.299
Oh, my. [chuckling]

01:04:25.800 --> 01:04:29.596
At this rate, your business might outshine
Myungsoondang overseas.

01:04:29.679 --> 01:04:32.182
Nonsense. [chuckling]

01:04:33.516 --> 01:04:36.936
-It's all thanks to my youngest daughter.
-[chuckles]

01:04:38.521 --> 01:04:43.318
Anyway, how's your son's business?

01:04:43.902 --> 01:04:45.111
What was it?

01:04:45.695 --> 01:04:48.615
I heard it was something to do with games.

01:04:48.698 --> 01:04:49.908
[chuckles sheepishly]

01:04:51.409 --> 01:04:54.871
[sighs softly] Every time I see him,
I think about

01:04:56.289 --> 01:04:57.624
how lucky people without kids are.

01:04:57.707 --> 01:04:58.708
[exclaims]`

01:04:59.792 --> 01:05:02.879
-[softly] It's because he's a son.
-[chuckles softly]

01:05:02.962 --> 01:05:06.132
Is our youngest daughter here
seeing someone?

01:05:06.216 --> 01:05:09.886
[hesitates] Do you have someone
to recommend?

01:05:09.969 --> 01:05:13.139
There's no need to look far
when the right one might be close by.

01:05:13.223 --> 01:05:14.557
Right.

01:05:14.641 --> 01:05:16.226
Let's check out the men from the company.

01:05:16.309 --> 01:05:17.477
-Right.
-Take a look.

01:05:17.560 --> 01:05:18.561
[Miyeon] Well...

01:05:19.020 --> 01:05:20.688
How about someone who runs a game company?

01:05:20.772 --> 01:05:22.732
-[Youngsook] Let's see.
-Me?

01:05:25.235 --> 01:05:28.988
"Now is a reading of the marriage vows
to celebrate the couple's union

01:05:29.072 --> 01:05:31.074
-and a congratulatory speech."
-[exclaims in amazement]

01:05:31.157 --> 01:05:33.201
-Hey, you look like the groom today.
-[chuckles]

01:05:33.284 --> 01:05:34.285
Thank you.

01:05:34.369 --> 01:05:36.287
But don't talk to me. I have to focus.

01:05:36.371 --> 01:05:38.414
Okay, fine.

01:05:38.498 --> 01:05:39.749
Don't make a mistake.

01:05:40.333 --> 01:05:42.543
-Do well.
-Okay, thanks.

01:05:42.627 --> 01:05:44.003
-[chuckles softly]
-[phone vibrating]

01:05:44.087 --> 01:05:45.338
[mumbles]

01:05:48.508 --> 01:05:49.717
Have you arrived?

01:05:50.009 --> 01:05:51.844
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

01:06:01.646 --> 01:06:02.855
[chuckles softly]

01:06:33.386 --> 01:06:34.470
[Eungsoo clears throat]

01:06:34.554 --> 01:06:36.222
We will now begin

01:06:36.306 --> 01:06:40.685
the wedding of Kim Wooju and Yoo Meri.

01:06:40.768 --> 01:06:44.814
Could all the guests please be seated?

01:06:45.648 --> 01:06:46.649
[clears throat]

01:06:47.233 --> 01:06:50.194
We will now begin the wedding ceremony

01:06:50.278 --> 01:06:53.448
of the groom, Mr. Kim Wooju,
and the bride, Ms. Yoo Meri.

01:06:54.032 --> 01:06:55.616
Bride and groom,

01:06:55.700 --> 01:06:58.119
prepare for your entrance.

01:06:58.202 --> 01:06:59.954
[♪ dreamy pop music playing]

01:07:05.084 --> 01:07:07.670
[Meri] Luck comes in disguise.

01:07:07.754 --> 01:07:08.921
[phone vibrating]

01:07:14.594 --> 01:07:15.595
Hello?

01:07:15.678 --> 01:07:18.431
When the greatest luck
of my life came to me...

01:07:18.514 --> 01:07:20.224
I won?

01:07:20.308 --> 01:07:22.352
But you're the only one I can turn to.

01:07:22.435 --> 01:07:24.520
Could you

01:07:24.604 --> 01:07:25.938
be my husband?

01:07:26.731 --> 01:07:29.192
I thought happiness
was finally coming my way,

01:07:30.526 --> 01:07:33.488
but luck built on lies can't be real.

01:07:35.114 --> 01:07:38.368
Maybe, in all those desperate moments
clinging to that house,

01:07:39.118 --> 01:07:41.412
what I truly wanted

01:07:42.955 --> 01:07:46.250
wasn't a fake home
I had to hide from everyone...

01:07:48.044 --> 01:07:52.632
but a single person who could love me
no matter who I was.

01:07:53.424 --> 01:07:55.343
It's because I like you.

01:07:55.426 --> 01:07:58.054
Whatever it is that you do,

01:07:58.137 --> 01:08:00.098
I'll stay right next to you.

01:08:02.433 --> 01:08:04.227
[Meri] Meeting someone like that.

01:08:06.312 --> 01:08:08.439
Isn't that what luck is really about?

01:08:11.067 --> 01:08:14.904
[Kim Wooju] Such luck comes like fate
in the most desperate moments.

01:08:22.995 --> 01:08:24.247
[crying]

01:08:25.081 --> 01:08:27.708
Who will take care of him?

01:08:27.792 --> 01:08:29.710
-Keep it.
-[teddy recording plays]

01:08:30.169 --> 01:08:31.879
[Kim Wooju] Some days were happy,

01:08:31.963 --> 01:08:33.965
and some days were not.

01:08:35.842 --> 01:08:38.719
Whenever waves of sorrow
and loneliness crashed over me,

01:08:39.971 --> 01:08:41.889
I lost my way and wandered.

01:08:43.724 --> 01:08:45.518
But maybe all that time

01:08:46.394 --> 01:08:49.689
was a path leading me to you.

01:08:55.153 --> 01:08:56.487
As if we had promised to meet

01:08:57.822 --> 01:08:59.449
after a long journey apart.

01:09:00.533 --> 01:09:02.368
[Meri] Every moment of our lives

01:09:03.744 --> 01:09:05.788
was leading us toward one another.

01:09:10.418 --> 01:09:11.419
I love you.

01:09:12.879 --> 01:09:13.880
I love you, too.

01:09:16.507 --> 01:09:18.718
[♪ wedding march playing on piano]

01:09:31.606 --> 01:09:33.649
[guests applauding, whooping]

01:09:40.364 --> 01:09:42.783
[♪ upbeat dreamy music playing]

01:09:55.630 --> 01:09:57.423
[guests continue applauding, whooping]

01:10:18.194 --> 01:10:19.987
[all cheering]

01:10:51.018 --> 01:10:53.688
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:11:37.732 --> 01:11:39.734
Translated by Susanna Kim